WHAT THIS ADDS
  A public, read-only GET /api/servers on the bot, so the website's Servers page
  (https://spinback-j7ao5f.camelai.app/servers.html) can list every Rust server the bot
  looks after: whatever the bot has measured, and "not reported" for anything it has not.

  The page reads /api/servers first and falls back to the public /api/status, so nothing
  breaks while this is unapplied - it just reports what the public status carries and says
  so on the page.

REVISED (this version)
  Step 1 previously read a "serverChecks" map and "state.guildInfo". Neither exists in
  bot/server.mjs any more, so that version would throw on the first request. This version
  reads the two things that do exist: settings.servers, and rconState - the last server
  that answered or refused an RCON command, which is the same record /api/status reports.
  rconState covers one server at a time, so a saved server that has not been contacted
  since the bot started is reported as unknown, never as offline.

WHERE
  bot/server.mjs, in the HTTP request handler, directly AFTER the existing
  'GET /api/guilds' block, above the settings-auth gate. Public and read-only: it
  publishes no address, no password and no token.

  serversCache must sit at MODULE scope, not inside the handler, or it resets every
  request and the cache does nothing:

    let serversCache = { at: 0, body: null };

CONTRACT THE PAGE EXPECTS
  Missing fields are printed as "not reported", never guessed.

  { "ok": true, "count": 1, "servers": [ {
      "id": "srv_1", "name": "Spinback 5X EU", "guild": "Spinback",
      "online": true, "state": "online", "ms": 38,
      "checkedAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z", "reason": null,
      "players": null, "maxPlayers": null, "map": null
  } ] }

  host and port are deliberately not sent. To publish them, add them to the object below
  and nothing on the site has to change.

STEP 1 - the minimal version: something the bot has already measured, no new connections
------------------------------------------------------------------------------- cut here
  /* Every Rust server the bot looks after, for the website's Servers page. Public and
     read-only on purpose: nothing here is not already reported to a browser by
     /api/status, and the address and password stay in the bot. */
  if (req.method === 'GET' && url === '/api/servers') {
    const cors = { 'content-type': 'application/json', 'cache-control': 'public, max-age=30',
      'access-control-allow-origin': '*' };
    if (!serversCache.body || Date.now() - serversCache.at > 30000) {
      const guild = GUILD_ID ? client.guilds.cache.get(GUILD_ID) : null;
      const list = (settings.servers || []).map(function (server) {
        const same = rconState && rconState.server
          && String(rconState.host || '') === String(server.host || '')
          && Number(rconState.port || 0) === Number(server.port || 0);
        return {
          id: String(server.id || ''),
          name: String(server.name || 'Rust server'),
          guild: guild ? guild.name : null,
          online: same ? rconState.ok === true : null,
          state: same ? (rconState.ok === true ? 'online' : 'offline') : 'unknown',
          ms: same && typeof rconState.ms === 'number' ? rconState.ms : null,
          checkedAt: same ? rconState.checkedAt : null,
          reason: same ? (rconState.ok ? null : (rconState.reason || 'unknown')) : 'not-checked-yet',
          detail: same ? null : 'This server has not been contacted since the bot started.',
          players: null,
          maxPlayers: null,
          map: null,
        };
      });
      serversCache = { at: Date.now(), body: JSON.stringify({ ok: true, count: list.length, servers: list }) };
    }
    res.writeHead(200, cors);
    res.end(serversCache.body);
    return;
  }
